# Changelog and versioning

- Each package is versioned independently (SemVer; pre-1.0 a MINOR bump is a new feature, a
  breaking class/token rename is also MINOR but must be called out as **Breaking**).
- `packages/<pkg>/CHANGELOG.md` has a `## X.Y.Z` heading per release, newest first, with
  bullets written for users: the class, token or utility name and what it now does.
- Bump with `npm version X.Y.Z --no-git-tag-version --workspace=<pkg>` so the lockfile stays
  in sync; changelog and version change in the same commit `release: <pkg> X.Y.Z`.
- Renaming or removing a public class, utility, token or data attribute is breaking. Prefer
  keeping the old name as an alias for one MINOR release.
